#### Systematic error study

The systematic errors contributing to the final total charm cross section were studied. One of the important sources is the uncertainty of charm hadron \(p_{T}\) spectrum and the fractions of different charm hadrons. The effect caused by the charm hadron \(p_{T}\) spectrum was studied by changing the power law parameters to \(1\sigma\) away. The correlations between parameters were not taken into account in the estimation, instead, we looped all the combinations to find the largest deviation as the estimation systematic uncertainty. The effect caused by the uncertain fractions of different charm hadrons was studied by changing the effective fraction in the decay \(D^{0}:D^{+}=0.79:0.21\) to \(0.90:0.10\) and \(0.70:0.30\). For the charm decaying to electron kinematics, the difference of two decay codes was take into the systematic errors. Table 3.6 shows the contributions from possible sources.

